' Use case diagram: Play Kana Wilds (Learner)
' The kana battle-and-catch game in the walkable world (docs/WORLD.md, docs/KANA-BATTLE.md).
' Sources: nihon-web/src/pages/KanaWildsPage.tsx, VillagePage.tsx, WildRoutePage.tsx, IslandScenePage.tsx;
' nihon-api/src/routes/kana-wilds.routes.ts.
' Sequence diagrams: 16 (battle and catch), 17 (challenge a challenger).
' On the Overall diagram, draw one use case "Play Kana Wilds" for the Learner.
@startuml UC Play Kana Wilds
title Play Kana Wilds (Learner)
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor Learner

rectangle "Play Kana Wilds" {
  usecase "Choose a starter kana" as Starter
  usecase "Walk the world\n(village, wild paths, islands)" as Walk
  usecase "Battle a wild kana" as Battle
  usecase "Defend against an attack\n(read the kana)" as Defend
  usecase "Catch a kana\n(trace its strokes)" as Catch
  usecase "Quick battle" as Quick
  usecase "View kana collection" as Collection
  usecase "Evolve a kana\n(か → が, き → きゃ)" as Evolve
  usecase "Challenge an island challenger" as Challenge
  usecase "Get a tip after a loss" as Tip
}

Learner --> Starter
Learner --> Walk
Learner --> Quick
Learner --> Collection
Learner --> Challenge

Walk <.. Battle : <<extend>>\n(step onto tall grass\nor rough water)
Battle ..> Defend : <<include>>
Catch ..> Battle : <<extend>>\n(enemy at or below 60% HP)
Quick ..> Battle : <<include>>
Challenge ..> Defend : <<include>>
Tip ..> Challenge : <<extend>>\n(lost or gave up)
Evolve ..> Collection : <<extend>>\n(level 3 + Sensei / Zen beaten)

note right of Starter : once, before anything else:\nか, さ or た plus the five vowels
note bottom of Challenge : Chun, Tama, Pon, Sensei, Zen, Kurama;\nthe first win pays XP and brings a reward
@enduml
